<p></p>
<p>Again, these are <em>projected</em> JPCs based on filing and population data current as of January 1, 2025.</p>    </div>
</section>
    <section class="hide-off-screen">
                <h3 class="h3"><span id="" class="jc-title">Additional Minor/Technical Changes</span></h3>
        <div>
            <p>In addition, the Maricopa County Elections Department had some very small changes to other voting precincts. In a redistricting effort after the 2020 census, several voting precincts were left with no voters in them. These are small areas of land known as "non-voting precincts", or NVPs which the Elections Department wished to merge into neighboring precincts that <em>do</em> have voters.</p>
<p>These changes did not affect Justice Court operations or case filings; eliminate these NVPs simplifies maps and data. They are as follows: </p>
<ol style="list-style-type: lower-alpha;">
<li>Move NVP 1 to South Mountain Justice Court in order to merge NVP 1 into South Mtn Park South VP.</li>
<li>Move NVP 2 to West Mesa Justice Court in order to merge NVP 2 into June VP.</li>
<li>Move NVP 5 to Kyrene Justice Court in order to merge NVP 5 into Pointe VP.</li>
<li>Move NVP 6 to Kyrene Justice Court in order to merge NVP 6 into Diablo VP.</li>
<li>Move NVP 7 to Kyrene Justice Court in order to merge NVP 7 into Diablo VP.</li>
<li>Move NVP 12 to Ironwood Justice Court in order to merge NVP 12 into Rainbow Valley VP.</li>
<li>Move NVP 13 to Ironwood Justice Court in order to merge NVP 13 into Salome VP.</li>
<li>Move NVP 14 to Hassayampa Justice Court in order to merge NVP 14 into Aguila VP.</li>
<li>Move NVP 15 to San Tan Justice Court in order to merge NVP 15 into Williams Field VP.</li>
<li>Move NVP 16 to Ironwood Justice Court in order to merge NVP 16 into Rainbow Valley VP.</li>
<li>Move NVP 17 to South Mountain Justice Court in order to merge NVP 17 into South Mtn Park SW VP.</li>
<li>Move NVP 18 to Agua Fria Justice Court in order to merge NVP 18 into Pee-Posh VP.</li>
<li>Move NVP 22 to Agua Fria Justice Court in order to merge NVP 22 into Komatke VP. (Gila River IC)</li>
</ol>
        </div>
    </section>



<section>
    <div class="jc-image-wrap">
        <span class="jc-image-center">
                <img role="img" class="jc-image-position jc-image" style="float:left; margin:0 1.4rem 1.4rem 0; padding-right:12px; width:33%;" src="/media/giyjj112/nvps.png?cc=0.00015615384615386135,0.0000000000000000568434188608,0.44246384615384615,0.0000000000000001136868377216&amp;width=899&amp;height=500&amp;rnd=133922155741530000" alt="Image of a search box with the text &#x27;Nvp 12 Voting Precinct&#x27; as the search text.">
        </span>
<p>You can use the Maricopa County Interactive Election District Map to search for any of these non-voting precincts.</p>
<p>Go to the web site below and in the search window on the left side of the page, enter "NVP [x]" as shown in the example image here.</p>
<p><a href="https://recorder.maricopa.gov/reviewer/default.htm" title="Maricopa County Interactive Election District Map" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Maricopa County Interactive Election District Map</a></p>    </div>
</section>


<section>
            <h3 class="h3"><span id="" class="jc-title">Public Presentations</span></h3>
    <div class="jc-image-wrap">
        <span class="jc-image-center">
                <img role="img" class="jc-image-position jc-image" style="float:right; margin:0 0 1.4rem 1.4rem; padding-left:12px; width:33%;" src="/media/nbshzjcd/gavel-and-keyboard.jpeg?width=899&amp;height=500&amp;rnd=133627557243430000" alt="Gavel and keyboard">
        </span>
<p>We did not suggest these changes lightly or alone. Court customers have a voice in the process.</p>
<p>The Maricopa County Justice Courts held two public meetings this summer to present this formally to the public and to take your questions. These public meetings were virtual on the Microsoft Teams platform to facilitate attendance by computer, tablet, or smart phone. These meetings were: </p>
<ul>
<li>Thursday, July 17th, 2025 at 7:10 p.m.  <span style="color: #bf0426;"><strong><a href="https://youtu.be/Ekts6stFo5o" title="Meeting 1 recording" target="_blank" style="color: #bf0426;" rel="noopener">Watch the recording</a></strong></span></li>
<li>Monday, August 4th, 2025 at 6 p.m.      <a href="https://youtu.be/pnZFt7ejr6c" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong><span style="color: #bf0426;">Watch the recording</span></strong></a></li>
</ul>
<p>Once those were done, we presented a similar plan to the Maricopa County Board of Supervisors for their vote:</p>
<ul>
<li>Monday, September 29th, 2025 at 10:30am   <span style="color: #bf0426;"><strong><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5wZ9Sbf3lwU" target="_blank" data-anchor="?v=5wZ9Sbf3lwU" style="color: #bf0426;" rel="noopener">Watch the Q&amp;A with the Supervisors</a></strong></span></li>
<li>Wednesday, October 1st, 2025 at 11:15am    <span style="color: #bf0426;"><strong><a href="https://youtu.be/WSZha_s5voI?t=5984" target="_blank" data-anchor="?t=5984" style="color: #bf0426;" rel="noopener">Watch the vote and public comment</a></strong></span></li>
</ul>    </div>
</section>
                  
